# Context allowlist for deploy/docker/cocoindex.Dockerfile (BuildKit reads the
# <Dockerfile>.dockerignore sitting next to the Dockerfile when -f is used).
#
# IMAGE HYGIENE (IP + slim), carried over from the retired pruned-mktemp
# context in onprem-deploy.yml: the build context must carry ONLY the Python
# pipeline + its lock — never the Next.js app, docs/, .planning/ (client IP),
# docs-site, .claude, or tests. Allowlist semantics: exclude everything, then
# re-include exactly what the Dockerfile COPYs. Last match wins.
*
!requirements.lock
!scripts/
scripts/*
!scripts/cocoindex_pipeline/
!scripts/bid_worker.py
!scripts/analyse_template.py
!scripts/extract_tender_questions.py
!scripts/docx_utils.py

# Test/corpus fixtures never ship in the image: the nightly seeds the walked
# corpus from the checkout (deploy/onprem/sync-platform-corpus.sh) and stages
# form templates via POST /stage — both read the repo, not the image.
scripts/cocoindex_pipeline/fixtures/

# Junk that would dirty layer hashes.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store
